Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::an_endpoint_context_keeps_each_field_in_its_own_bits`.

The defect: `endpoint` drops the mask on the endpoint type and shifts it one bit too far, so the type lands in bits 4 to 6. Codes 4 to 7 spill into the reserved bit 6, and the code read back from bits 3 to 5 is wrong. Dropping the mask alone leaves the harness green, since every `EndpointType` code fits three bits, so the patch also moves the field to give the spill a place to go.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that bits 3 to 5 of dword 1 hold the endpoint type's code, and its check that bits 6 to 15 are zero.

diff --git a/src/context.rs b/src/context.rs
--- a/src/context.rs
+++ b/src/context.rs
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
     };
     [
         (interval as u32) << 16,
-        3 << 1 | (kind as u32 & 0x7) << 3 | (maximum_packet as u32) << 16,
+        3 << 1 | (kind as u32) << 4 | (maximum_packet as u32) << 16,
         dequeue as u32,
         (dequeue >> 32) as u32,
         average_transfer_request_block_bytes as u32 | maximum_service_interval_payload << 16,
